entries.body:
NL8001 now warns when a UTF-16 offset into a non-ASCII string is the answer of a data-parallel body (parallelMap, parallelMapInto, parallelFrom, parallelReduce), an index into anything but a string, parallelFrom's count, a loop bound, a call argument, or a helper's return value. The walk follows an offset into callees and out through returns, up to four call hops.

It stays quiet in these cases:
- an offset is compared only with another offset;
- a loop is bounded by its own cursor, alone or moved by a constant;
- a call passes a provably ASCII string to a parameter that is never written;
- an arrow captures a string that is provably ASCII;
- the offset goes back into a string method.

A code unit used as an array index or as parallelFrom's count also warns.

The walk is a lint, not a proof. It is silent past four calls, into generic functions or other modules, at a parameter the callee never reads, and at a spawn answer. docs/LANGUAGE.md lists these gaps.

Fixes #629
